  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">St Alberts Leaving NoOne Behind Chiwenga and Chadereka Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will be implemented by St Alberts in Chadereka and Chiwenga wards. The project focus is leave no one behind in resilient livelihoods, gender-based violence, drug, alcohol and substance abuse and child abuse mitigation. 
This project shall lead to the following outcomes:
I.	Community structures propel gender transformation and social accountability for positive behaviour towards child protection and gender justice.
II.	Women and youths are economically empowered through integrated livelihoods for improved socio-economic wellbeing of the most vulnerable groups.
III.	Communities prioritize mental health and responsible lifestyle through drug and substance abuse mitigation strategies. 
An MOU is in place covering 2023-2027 to guide operations in the district and working with traditional and religious leaders, through community-based structures. Livelihoods interventions will be guided by need and technical experts in the Province..</narrative>
  </description>
